{
  "storyId": "B-5a15",
  "name": "u03-causal-evidence-dag-transaction",
  "title": "U-03 CausalEvidence DAG: unique execution keys, CAS receipts, and precise freshness invalidation",
  "description": "Implement the P0-3 / U-03 item from docs/requirements/decisions/cross-story-agent-session-performance-root-causes-and-prioritized-optimization-plan.md: a CausalEvidence DAG with transactional persistence. Today intent, command execution, selector, material identity, and canonical evidence commit are not layered, so coarse hashes stale unrelated results and a failed Git/metadata commit discards already-PASS command output. This story makes identical execution keys run once with immutable receipt fan-out, writes CAS receipts before canonical import, and invalidates only declared dependency domains. It must not implement ReviewConvergence (U-01), ManagedRunSupervisor (U-02), or dependency-scoped re-review (U-09), must not rewrite stored hashes, and must keep materialHash plus the current strict DONE-required policy.",
